amages caused by errors or omissions in the original data set. BOEM has made efforts to ensure the accuracy and reliability of the data; however, some errors may exist. Notifications of errors are appreciated and shall be reported to the BOEM Office of Public Affairs (see contact information below). Data is not intended to be used as legal documentation and shall not be constructed as such. The data was developed within the U.S. Government; no proprietary rights may be attached to them nor may they be sold to the U.S. Government as part of any procurement of ADP products or services. Data is not to be used for navigational purposes.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;For more information please visit our webpage: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;A href="http://www.boem.gov/"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;https://www.boem.gov/&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Office of Public Affairs, Gulf of America OCS Region&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;1201 Elmwood Park Blvd. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;New Orleans, LA 70123-2394&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Phone: 1-800-200-4853&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</useLimit></Consts></resConst><idAbs>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;This file is based on the BOEM - Geospatial Services Division’s Official Protraction Diagram (OPD) and Leasing Maps (LM). The OPDs and LMs and Supplemental Official Block Diagrams (SOBDs) serve as the legal definition for BOEM offshore boundary coordinates and area descriptions. OPDs are numbered using the United Nations International Map of the World Numbering System, and are generally named for land or hydrographic features contained within the limits of the diagram. The use of OPDs and LMs makes it easier to refer to individual blocks within a region or planning area. Leasing Maps are part of an older system still in use in the Gulf of America. OPDs were built where existing oil and gas leases, at the time, had not yet occurred and where LMs had not yet been established. This data set contains Official Protraction Diagram (OPD) and Leasing Map (LM) outlines in ESRI shape file formats for the BOEM Gulf of America Region. In order to produce a file containing all the OPDs in a region – Official UTM OPDs and State Plane projected LM outlines were re-projected to basic geographic NAD27 unprojected space in order to create a continuous file. Because GIS projection and topology functions can change or generalize coordinates, these GIS files are NOT an OFFICIAL record for the exact OPD or LM boundaries. Only the official projected paper OPD or LM or a digital image (pdf) of them serves as OFFICIAL records. These can be found at the following location: https://www.boem.gov/Official-Protraction-Diagrams.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN /&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</idAbs><searchKeys><keyword>Bureau of Ocean Energy Management</keyword><keyword>BOEM</keyword><keyword>Outer Continental Shelf</keyword><keyword>OCS</keyword><keyword>Gulf of America</keyword><keyword>GOA</keyword><keyword>Submerged Lands Act Boundary</keyword><keyword>SLA</keyword><keyword>Federal</keyword><keyword>Oil</keyword><keyword>Gas</keyword><keyword>OCS Lease Blocks</keyword><keyword>Blocks</keyword><keyword>Alabama</keyword><keyword>Florida</keyword><keyword>Lousiana</keyword><keyword>Mississippi</keyword><keyword>Texas</keyword></searchKeys><idPurp>This and other cadastre information the BOEM products are generated in accordance with 30 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) Part 550.4 Subpart D, (formerly Part 556.8 Subpart A (2015)) to support Federal land ownership and mineral resource management.</idPurp><dataExt xmlns=""><geoEle xmlns=""><GeoBndBox esriExtentType="search"><exTypeCode>1</exTypeCode><westBL>-97.21133006125184</westBL><eastBL>-81.13759362840798</eastBL><southBL>23.822796757299255</southBL><northBL>30.246203